p.src:
Spacetime is difficult to picture, so replace the timelike direction by an ordinary angular direction. Write $\begin{aligned}
d\ell^2&=F(\rho)^2d\theta^2+d\rho^2,\\
F(\rho)&\sim
\begin{cases}
\rho, & \rho\to0,\\
4GM, & \rho\to\infty.
\end{cases}
\end{aligned}$ Near $\rho=0$, this is the plane in polar coordinates. Far away, the circumference no longer grows with radius: $C_\infty=\int_0^{2\pi}4GM\,d\theta=8\pi GM.$ The surface therefore rounds off at one end and approaches a cylinder at the other. It looks like a cigar.

